# Copy to the device-private `lolly/mcp-deploy.env` described in README.md and fill in.
# deploy.sh validates and sources that file; never put the filled copy in this checkout.

# ── required ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PROJECT_ID=your-gcp-project-id

# Retrieve the bearer/OAuth passphrase from the team's managed secret store.
LOLLY_MCP_TOKEN=paste-the-lolly-mcp-token

# Retrieve the OAuth signing key from the managed store, or mint a replacement
# there with `openssl rand -base64 32` and rotate the old deployment value.
LOLLY_MCP_SIGNING_SECRET=paste-the-signing-secret

# Token for a Redis-compatible HTTPS REST endpoint (for example an Upstash
# database). The URL is not secret; the token is stored in Secret Manager.
# Hosted deployments refuse to start without this cross-instance limiter.
LOLLY_RATE_LIMIT_REST_URL=https://your-rate-limit-store.example.com
LOLLY_RATE_LIMIT_REST_TOKEN=paste-the-rate-limit-token

# Sole issuer/resource origin used in OAuth metadata and bearer challenges.
# Use the mapped domain if one exists; it must be https and have no path/query.
LOLLY_MCP_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://mcp.example.com

# ── optional (sensible defaults) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# REGION=us-central1
# SERVICE=lolly-mcp
# AR_REPO=lolly
# LOLLY_WEB_BASE=https://lolly.tools   # web shell the container drives for Tier B
# Exact extra HTTPS origins Chromium may contact, comma-separated. The web-shell
# origin is always included. Leave empty unless an instance really needs one.
# LOLLY_BROWSER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://assets.example.com
# LOLLY_BROWSER_MAX_CONCURRENCY=2      # active Chromium contexts per instance
# LOLLY_BROWSER_MAX_QUEUE=8            # bounded waiters; overflow is refused
# LOLLY_BROWSER_QUEUE_TIMEOUT_MS=30000 # refuse a stale queued request
# LOLLY_MCP_RPM=120                    # authorised MCP requests per bearer/minute
# LOLLY_OAUTH_RPM=30                   # OAuth requests per client/minute
